    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "All **70 tests pass** with `BUILD SUCCESS`. The change is complete and green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI released version 2 of the owner identity. The DTOs are generated from `openapi.yml`, so I changed the spec and the code that populates/derives the affected values.\n\n**Identity derivation (V2 region tag inside identifiers)** \u2014 `OwnerRestControllerV1`:\n- Added `IDENTITY_VERSION_TAG = \"V2\"` and `regionCodeV2(city, postcode)` = `\"V2\" + deriveRegion(...)`.\n- `memberId` now uses the V2 region as its `<REGION>` prefix (e.g. `V2NSW27...`).\n- `householdId` folds the V2 region into its SHA-256 preimage.\n- `identityKey` (`identityKeyFor`, plus the mapper's `deriveIdentityKey`) appends the V2 region to its preimage. Duplicate detection and soft-match paths were updated to compute each owner's V2 region so identical owners still collide and same-household owners still share an id. Every identifier changes; no V1 value recurs.\n\n**User-facing region stays plain** \u2014 `locality`, `timezone`, and the owner-segment region still use the untagged region (e.g. `NSW`), verified by Cp55 (`STANDARD_METRO`).\n\n**Response shape** \u2014 `openapi.yml`: moved `memberId`/`householdId`/`identityKey` into a new nested `OwnerIdentity` schema referenced as `identity`, and added a top-level integer `apiVersion` (2). `OwnerMapper` builds the `identity` object and sets `apiVersion`.\n\n**Audit schema v2** \u2014 `emitOwnerCreatedEvent` now emits `schemaVersion: 2`, carries the V2 `memberId`, and recomputes `ownerSegment` from the version-2 identity.\n\nRequest fields are unchanged. All existing and new (Cp52/53/55/56/57/60, etc.) tests pass.",
