    "probe_text": "Here's the complete, ordered sequence for `POST /api/owners`. The request first passes through framework-level Bean Validation on the request body, then the controller (`OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`) runs a long chain of validations and side-effects inline (the service layer itself is just a pass-through `save`).\n\n## Phase 0 \u2014 Before the method body runs\n\n1. **Security check** \u2014 `@PreAuthorize(\"hasRole(@roles.OWNER_ADMIN)\")`. Caller must hold `OWNER_ADMIN` (else 403/401).\n2. **Bean Validation on the `@Valid @RequestBody OwnerFieldsDto`** \u2014 a violation here throws `MethodArgumentNotValidException` \u2192 **400** before any controller logic:\n   - `firstName`: `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..30)`, `@Pattern` (letters, up to 2 separators)\n   - `lastName`: `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..30)`, `@Pattern`\n   - `title`: `@Size(1..10)`\n   - `address` / `addressLine1` / `addressLine2`: `@Size(1..255)`\n   - `city`: `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..80)`\n   - `telephone`: `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..20)`\n   - `email`: `@Size(max 255)`, `@Email`\n   - `postcode`: `@Pattern(^[0-9]{4}$)`\n\n## Phase 1 \u2014 Controller body, in execution order\n\n3. **Idempotency replay check** \u2014 if an `Idempotency-Key` header matches a prior create in the in-memory `idempotentCreates` map, return the stored DTO with **200** (short-circuits everything below).\n4. **Address composition & normalization** *(side-effect)* \u2014 prefers `addressLine1`/`addressLine2` (each normalized) over the flat `address`; composes the final `address` string.\n5. **`rejectMissingOrBlankFields`** \u2014 validates required fields aren't blank after composition \u2192 `MissingOwnerFieldsException` **400**.\n6. **`rejectCityAtCapacity`** \u2014 rejects if the city already has \u2265 50 owners \u2192 `CityAtCapacityException` **409**.\n7. **`ownerMapper.toOwner(...)`** *(side-effect)* \u2014 maps DTO \u2192 `Owner` entity (ignores `id`/`pets`).\n8. **Set normalized address fields** *(side-effect)* \u2014 `address`, `addressLine1`, `addressLine2`.\n9. **`normalizeTelephone`** \u2014 validates + normalizes to E.164 \u2192 `InvalidTelephoneException` **400**; sets `telephone` *(side-effect)*.\n10. **`normalizeEmail`** \u2014 validates + lower-cases \u2192 `InvalidEmailException` **400**; sets `email` *(side-effect)*.\n11. **`validatePostcode(city, postcode)`** \u2014 city/postcode consistency \u2192 `InvalidPostcodeException` **400**.\n12. **Derive `regionV2`** and **`householdId`** *(side-effect, computed)*.\n13. **`rejectDuplicateIdentity`** \u2014 unified identity-collision check (telephone / email / lastname+region) \u2192 `DuplicateTelephoneException` **409**.\n14. **`rejectFutureRegistrationDate`** \u2014 \u2192 `FutureRegistrationDateException` **400**.\n15. **Registration date defaulting & business-day roll-forward** *(side-effect)* \u2014 defaults to `LocalDate.now()` if absent, then `toBusinessDay` rolls off weekends/holidays.\n16. **`rejectDailyOwnerLimit`** \u2014 rejects if \u2265 100 owners already registered for that date \u2192 `DailyOwnerLimitExceededException` **429**.\n17. **Set derived/warning fields** *(side-effects)* \u2014 `bulkSignupWarning`, `capacityWarning`, `registrationDate`, `memberId` (region+FY+SHA+Luhn, de-duplicated), `householdId`, `namesakeCount`, `householdMemberCount`.\n18. **Membership computation** *(side-effects)* \u2014 `membershipPoints`, then `membershipLevel` (capped by household unless `sharesHousehold` is true).\n19. **Duplicate-detection flags** *(side-effects)* \u2014 `possibleDuplicate` / `possibleDuplicateOf`.\n20. **`clinicService.saveOwner(owner)`** *(side-effect \u2014 persistence)* \u2014 pass-through to `ownerRepository.save(...)`.\n21. **Audit log line** *(side-effect)* \u2014 `AUDIT.info(\"owner created ...\")`.\n22. **`emitOwnerCreatedEvent`** *(side-effect)* \u2014 serializes an `OWNER_CREATED` JSON event with a monotonic sequence number and logs it (SLF4J only \u2014 not a Spring `ApplicationEvent`).\n23. **Welcome-notification log line** *(side-effect)* \u2014 `NOTIFY.info(\"welcome owner ...\")` (log only \u2014 no real email/messaging).\n24. **`ownerMapper.toOwnerDto(owner)`** *(side-effect)* \u2014 maps to response DTO, deriving many read-only fields.\n25. **Store idempotency result** *(side-effect)* \u2014 if an `Idempotency-Key` was supplied, cache the DTO for future replay.\n26. **Set `Location` header** and return **201 Created**.\n\n## Notes worth flagging\n\n- **No password hashing and no real email/notification.** SHA-256 appears only for deriving `memberId`/`householdId`/identity keys; \"notify\"/\"audit\"/\"event\" are all just SLF4J log lines.\n- **The service layer does nothing but `save`** \u2014 all validation and side-effect logic lives in the controller.\n- The **entity-level constraints** on `Owner` (`@NotEmpty` on `address`/`city`/`telephone`, E.164 `@Pattern`) and on `Person` (`firstName`/`lastName`) are *not* what validates the request; `@Valid` targets the DTO. They'd only fire if the JPA provider runs validation on flush.\n- `DuplicateEmailException` / `DuplicateHouseholdException` handlers exist but are no longer thrown on this path (subsumed by the unified identity check in step 13)."
